.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 423 AM PDT Mon Aug 24 2026

Mixed bag of VFR/IFR/LIFR early this morning. Status filled north
into KSTS and is expected to lift by mid morning with VFR expected
to prevail across the Bay Area terminals and inland South Bay
airports. IFR/LIFR ceilings over Monterey Bay will give way to VFR
late morning, with IFR ceilings returning before sunset.

Vicinity of SFO...Low stratus lingers in vicinity of the terminals
but not expected to impact ceilings with VFR expected to prevail
throughout the day into the evening hours with MVFR/IFR expected
to develop around midnight.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar as SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...A relatively normal diurnal cycle of
IFR/LIFR ceilings expected through the forecast period, with
current IFR/LIFR ceilings expected to lift by late morning and
return in the early evening hours before sunset. Expect periods of
breezy onshore flow in the afternoon.

